WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:02.621
Open the battery-charger sample: a complete drawing set, 27 pages.

2
00:00:02.871 --> 00:00:06.745
The cover sheet: every sheet with its revision, issue status and the customer's approval.

3
00:00:06.995 --> 00:00:13.214
Place a contactor coil from the library: its designation is assigned by itself.

4
00:00:13.464 --> 00:00:23.277
Place its contact: same device, and the cross-references appear on both.

5
00:00:23.527 --> 00:00:25.873
Give the device a part from the library: the BOM will know about it.

6
00:00:26.123 --> 00:00:30.583
Number the wires with your own pattern: 020L+, 021L+ ...

7
00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:32.906
The wire list follows the schematic ...

8
00:00:33.156 --> 00:00:35.719
... and the BOM already counts the new contactor.

9
00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:40.385
Draw a wire that connects to nothing: the check banner finds it at once.

10
00:00:40.635 --> 00:00:42.180
One click on the fix, and the problem is gone.

11
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.554
PLC I/O: every channel with address, tag and what it is wired to.

12
00:00:44.804 --> 00:00:50.488
Edit a tag here, export the tag list for the PLC tool.

13
00:00:50.738 --> 00:00:52.222
Export the PDF drawing set ...

14
00:00:52.472 --> 00:00:54.698
... and every list as one XLSX workbook.

15
00:00:54.948 --> 00:01:03.757
Sizing: the motor is raised to 7.5 kW and the feeder is sized from the schematic.

16
00:01:04.007 --> 00:01:06.739
The contactor that meets the requirement and is in stock, with warehouse and location: select and confirm.

17
00:01:06.989 --> 00:01:10.501
The BOM shows the new part with on hand, available and location.

18
00:01:10.751 --> 00:01:16.154
Cabinet layout: suggest the whole layout. It is a preview, with the rules it applied.

19
00:01:16.404 --> 00:01:20.150
Accept it, then move a device: it snaps onto its DIN rail.

20
00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:26.857
The same cabinet in 3D, devices as boxes from their dimensions.

21
00:01:27.107 --> 00:01:31.784
The CAD workspace: type L, then coordinates, and the line is drawn.

22
00:01:32.034 --> 00:01:33.643
Object snap: the cursor locks on the end of the line and says so.

23
00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:42.327
The assistant, with your own API key: ask in plain words. It reads the page, searches the library and sizes with the sizing engine.

24
00:01:42.577 --> 00:01:45.917
A preview with a source on every claim; ratings are library parts and suggestions to confirm. Accept is one undo step, and so is undo. (This recording uses a scripted stand-in.)

25
00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.615
CablePilot: free, open source, your files stay yours.
